# Serve the dashboard's index.php for /admin/ and /admin
DirectoryIndex index.php

# NOTE: do NOT add `AddHandler application/x-httpd-php .php` here. The site
# root and /api execute PHP via the host's default handler (no AddHandler is
# set there). Forcing the legacy `application/x-httpd-php` token on hosts that
# use a different one (LiteSpeed / PHP-FPM / cPanel EA-PHP) leaves Apache with
# no processor for .php, so it serves index.php as a *download* instead of
# running it. /admin/ must inherit the same working handler as the rest of the
# site — which it does when we stay silent here.
